mortal kombat legends battle of the  realms it's a study in contrast it says  too much plot going on but it also has  awesome action ninjas and the voice of  joel mchale here are all the best and  worst things about mortal kombat legends  battle of the realms  johnny cage is a mortal kombat mainstay  going back to the very first entry of  the hit game series he brings to life a  strong hero archetype bravado and a  sense of humor as well looking at the  discussions around his absence on the  recent live-action film and the fans  desires to see him portrayed by the  right actor it all shows how important  he can be to any project in the  franchise joel mchale was a shining part  of the previous mk animated movie  scorpion's revenge and he continues that  streak as one of the best characters in  battle of the realms his relationship  with sonia blade and the levity he  offers is amusing without taking away  from what's going on around him mikhail  has spoken about how he improvised with  his scenes and that may have helped make  some of his moments more genuine and  funnier the only complaint of course is  that cage never secures that big win in  this adventure but he's still a  memorable part of the earth realm  defenders even while being a bit of a  jerk  there are many different realms in the  mortal kombat law several smaller ones  and six primary welds but it's rare that  any others than earth realm outworld and  netherrealm get to play much of a part  in the adventures even in denia where  several characters hail from is usually  relegated to a mention or the tiniest  flashback worlds like chaos realm and  sado are barely mentioned even in the  newer games having become afterthoughts  and the character endings for the most  part this also means that smaller realms  the law has introduced like vague ernest  zotero anyak and architect have little  chance of ever being relevant battle of  the realm still has a story that lives  up to the name but it seems silly now to  have hoped the film would have seen our  heroes go to these places or even give  us new information on them seeing our  champions jump across wells for the  various fights would have been quite the  trees but even on the worlds that were  used there weren't many new details to  be glimpsed even some of the newest  spots from the movie look as if they  were taken directly from the games such  as the shots of chinook's chambers  apparently directly inspired by the  in-game cut scenes from the conquest  mode of mortal kombat armageddon  scorpion's revenge gave fans a wonderful  look at the key parts of shang tsung's  island but the sequel film opened the  battlefield up a bit offering animators  a chance to show off some areas with  which players of the games have become  quite familiar the majority of battle of  the realms takes place in outworld but  beginning portions show off a few  locales on earth brief interludes in  netherrealm the meeting place of the  elder gods and an incredible exercise in  colour toward the end as realms begin to  merge most of these are gorgeous  backgrounds and help bring their  individual parts of the story to life  most notable on earth is a lin kuei  temple a site that has been shown in  different forms before but can never be  explored thoroughly enough the audience  sees a slow long shot of the main  structure the outside courtyard and to  look at the inner sanctum of the grand  master warm radiance containing statues  of famous linguay warriors it all ties  together the foreboding feeling the  scene presents in elsewhere the  participants expressed how intimidating  shao khan's fortresses and a brief  glimpse of his throne room shows off  that awesome green hue behind him there  is a lot of detail put into the arena  where most of the fighting takes place  these are all solid representations of  the stages mostly inspired by the newer  games but the extra bits help make the  worlds feel more alive  one of the awesome things that the last  couple of mortal kombat games did was  progress the overall narrative giving  fans new events and lore to chuwan with  the subject matter for battle of the  realms there was hope that the film  would give us fresh tidbits of lore or  clarify some of the existing meta plot  this isn't just to learn more about the  realms but i hope that fans could see  deeper backgrounds for various  characters or some progression in the  relationships they share none of this  really happens however with the  exception of lu kang which is only a  brief moment that shows the death of his  parents what was that even connected to  and why were those tar cartons on earth  hunting them down those with a truly  extensive knowledge of mortal kombat  could potentially fill in some gaps but  not all of what fans tend to believe is  also considered to be canon so a film  adaptation like this presents an  interesting opportunity to firm up  aspects of the series lore the real miss  prospect here is not providing anything  new about the elder gods the newer  titans or especially the one being who  plays a pivotal role at the end true the  one being is supposed to be a mysterious  figure that no one truly comprehends but  it seems like the writers purposefully  guided the plot around him perhaps so  they wouldn't have to answer any  questions or say something new it's a  shame and it feels like this promising  alternate story though full of passion  falls short of doing anything truly  spectacular  although the last one did a fair job in  delivering on violence and bloodshed  battle of the realms pushed it just a  bit further mortal kombat is a series  that needs to embrace its more vicious  tendencies to feel at home judging by  the creativity in some of these murders  they are loving the recent r ratings  audiences will see some brutal finishes  and a couple of interesting takes on  classic fatalities but a large portion  of the carnage comes from the standard  fighting dispatching grunts in the most  over-the-top way possible not only is  there a ton of decapitations bone  breaking and the ripping out of  perfectly good body parts but the first  act takes advantage of an army of  disposable soldiers we see shots linger  more when some of this happens and much  of the art and animation choices around  these attacks are meant to accent the  savagery each fighter possesses when  pushed this leads to the use of more  x-ray moves that never overstay their  welcome  one of the problems with movies like  this is the desire to throw in as many  extra characters as possible sometimes  because it'll get fans excited to see  one of their low-key favorites but more  often than not they are in there because  the script needed someone to take a loss  or eat a fatality for this instalment it  seems like stryker and jade took that  bullet both are introduced by name get  some lines and do absolutely nothing  else worth mentioning jay's relation to  katana isn't brought up at all and she  gets her skull cracked open by sonia  early on and then knocked off screen  with an impressive uppercut from liu  kang never to be seen again striker at  least gets a little bit more time to  shine he may be the new guy but he's  also a capable hero and he at least  receives a beautifully disgusting death  scene still these are two characters  that feel wasted and would have  benefited from more moments focused on  them scorpion and sub-zero are two of  the most iconic characters in the mortal  kombat franchise but players have a soft  spot for all of the various  pilot-swapped ninja characters from the  games though scorpion's revenge gave us  the classic origin of the iconic ninja  duo fans are excited to see the sequel  bring in cyrax sector smoke and of  course the younger sub-zero kwai liang  who's seeking revenge for his dead  brother these characters are all badass  and each given at least a brief moment  to shine having their own storyline  going on outside other tournaments but  with their robotic arsenals and  elemental powers their fights almost  steal the show that's right the battle  of the realms crams a cyber initiative  story arc into a few spectacular scenes  many of these characters fight together  and against each other giving fans a lot  to observe especially when fighters like  scorpion and sub-zero begin using their  powers together but for many the coolest  bit is getting to see smoke in action  building up the friendship and respect  he has for kwai liang and watching the  story unfold after his change it's hard  not to wish for more of it but their  mission eventually had to feed into the  bigger plot and take the focus off of  those incredibly cool ninja characters  scorpion's revenge had its flaws but  overall it pleased fans and gave them a  reason to believe a sequel would deliver  the goods while battle of the realms  might be an adequate follow-up  especially if only considering the first  two acts something about the ending just  doesn't sit right it isn't horrible but  it's nowhere near the quality of the  rest of the film the third act is much  crazier which is expected but feels like  it's from a different movie  predominantly because of the two main  fights the final battle against shin arc  has a ton of moving parts and is on a  much grander scale with god-like powers  being thrown around this makes sense but  it loses a lot of the intensity not to  mention the blood of the previous  encounters even if the stakes are sky  high no one can call this anticlimactic  a little boring perhaps but there should  be some negative points awarded for only  having a slightly better version of the  ending from mortal kombat annihilation  with the giant dragon and everything the  fight between lukang and xiao khan may  be worse however some of the moves look  like they were lifted directly from  dragon ball z but without the extra  power levels to help it make sense both  of these encounters needed to stay a bit  more grounded to stick the landing  many of the mortal kombat characters  have found their voices over the  lifespan of the series though the actors  who portray them often change even if  what's coming out of the combatant's  mouth might not be a perfect recreation  of recent games none of the voices in  either of the two modern animated movies  have felt bad enough to stand out so  many of the talents who helped bring the  cast to life in scorpion's revenge  return to play the characters again  which is a testament to how well they  did and a great number of the voice  actors filled their parts perfectly with  many of them playing multiple roles it's  always fun to hear words like kami dogu  and outworld uttered with such  seriousness and precision new voices mix  well with the old forming a bloody  chorus of grunts and screams that work  perfectly for the film  animated features are typically shorter  than the live-action counterparts but  battle of the realms clocks in it right  under 90 minutes it's about nine minutes  longer than his predecessor which again  tried to cram too much into his plot and  here it's obvious that wb didn't learn  from their earlier mistake the idea of  not overstaying your welcome is  certainly admirable but why throw so  much into the mix if that's the plan  there's enough platia for two  feature-length projects making matters  even more overstuffed than scorpion's  revenge the champions of earth realm  going to a final tournament in outworld  feels like a plot that easily could have  filled 90 minutes but piled on top of  that it's all the drama of the other  stories too it'd be easy to go trim the  fat saving the kami dogu and the one  being for a follow-up tale when a true  final boss was required however  screenwriter jeremy adams has implied  that the mortal kombat legends films  were a two-chapter story meaning they  had to put everything in because there  might not be others to come if true that  is a huge shame as doing so may have  hindered the overall story and fans  would have likely welcomed further  animated films in the mortal kombat  universe check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite movies and tv  shows are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

